1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:05,046
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:12,387
[Emilia] <i>Natalie, tell me.</i>

3
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:14,973
<i>Is he being considered</i>
<i>by the party to run for Senate?</i>

4
00:00:15,056 --> 00:00:16,975
<i>Yes, he is. I thought you already knew.</i>

5
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:18,810
<i>I'm a man of my words, Miss Aguas.</i>

6
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:19,936
<i>I hope you are, too.</i>

7
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,146
[Natalie] <i>You just won't stop</i>

8
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:22,856
<i>flirting with my boyfriend, will you?</i>

9
00:00:22,939 --> 00:00:26,151
<i>Choose. Ivy, or my daddy's support</i>

10
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:28,361
<i>for your senatorial ambitions?</i>

11
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:29,988
<i>Why are you so selfish?!</i>

12
00:00:30,071 --> 00:00:31,740
<i>Have you forgotten that we're a family?</i>

13
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:32,991
<i>We should help each other</i>

14
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:34,659
<i>instead of going against one another!</i>

15
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,870
<i>Lily, where are you?!</i>

16
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:38,329
<i>-I miss you so much!</i>
<i>-If I were Lily,</i>

17
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:42,792
<i>I would probably say,</i>
<i>"Diego, you have to move on</i>

18
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:44,919
<i>because we lead different lives now."</i>

19
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:46,254
-[gunshot]
-[Lily screams]

20
00:00:46,337 --> 00:00:47,380
<i>Sorry, did I interrupt you?</i>

21
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:50,008
<i>I saw an animal, but I missed it.</i>

22
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:51,634
[Emilia] <i>Arnaldo doesn't know</i>

23
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:53,261
<i>that Papa already gave that to me,</i>

24
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:55,180
<i>so I had it transferred under my name.</i>

25
00:00:55,263 --> 00:00:57,724
[Ivy] <i>I'm still buying</i>
<i>your overpriced property.</i>

26
00:00:57,807 --> 00:00:59,934
<i>But let me just remind you, Emilia,</i>

27
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:04,355
<i>I don't like any of my friends</i>
<i>using me for my money.</i>

28
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:06,191
<i>Your happy days are over, Tonio.</i>

29
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:07,859
<i>It's time for you to talk.</i>

30
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:09,486
<i>I'm already fed up with you.</i>

31
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:12,280
-<i>Let him eat.</i>
-[grunts]

32
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:14,741
<i>He won't get far. I'll take care of him.</i>

33
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:16,910
[Belen] <i>Raul, you need to get back here.</i>

34
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,953
<i>She's coming back to her senses.</i>

35
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:20,330
<i>Where are you going?</i>

36
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:22,082
<i>I'm going to take care</i>
<i>of our gambling business.</i>

37
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:23,833
<i>The senator already gave me the go signal.</i>

38
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:26,961
<i>I don't care if the devil</i>
<i>himself gave you the go.</i>

39
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:29,130
<i>If I tell you to stay,</i>
<i>you're going to stay.</i>

40
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:31,758
<i>If I want to leave this house,</i>
<i>then I will!</i>

41
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:33,301
<i>Raul!</i>

42
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:37,514
[suspenseful music playing]

43
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:40,016
[Belen] <i>She's coming back to her senses.</i>

44
00:01:48,566 --> 00:01:49,734
[exhales]

45
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,946
[car engine rumbling]

46
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:54,405
[scoffs]

47
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:57,283
Damn you, Emilia.

48
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:01,246
[Emilia] I've read the draft
of the publicity materials.

49
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:03,832
I like it. Have it published already.

50
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:05,208
All right.

51
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:11,840
I can't believe it. Is there
really no hope for you two?

52
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:14,092
I'm really disappointed.

53
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:18,096
But, Auntie, you did a great job
watching over him!

54
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:20,348
As you can see, I gave you a bonus.

55
00:02:20,431 --> 00:02:23,643
Oh! I saw the two designer bags
in my room.

56
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:26,312
You're very generous, Emilia.

57
00:02:27,438 --> 00:02:30,358
Well, Auntie, it's because I'm
a hundred-fifty-million richer.

58
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:33,153
-That's thanks to Miss Aguas.
-[Claire chuckles]

59
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:35,697
She's so gullible. [laughs]

60
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,867
Now you got me curious.
I want to meet this woman.

61
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,660
Soon, you will, Auntie.

62
00:02:40,743 --> 00:02:42,829
But not just yet because I'll be busy,

63
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:44,622
and I need you to run the house.

64
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,374
Starting tomorrow,

65
00:02:47,041 --> 00:02:50,003
my senatorial dreams
will slowly be coming true.

66
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:52,338
[giggles]

67
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:59,012
[pants]

68
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:00,555
[grunts]

69
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:07,312
[suspenseful music playing]

70
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:12,275
[panting]

71
00:03:16,154 --> 00:03:17,447
[map alert pings]

72
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:19,532
[mockingly] Tonio…

73
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,372
You sure you wanna play hide and seek?

74
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,292
[map alert pings]

75
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:37,550
[tense music swells]

76
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:45,308
Get up!

77
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:53,233
Did you think you could get away from me?

78
00:03:53,858 --> 00:03:55,610
How did you find me here?

79
00:03:57,528 --> 00:03:58,529
<i>Sit down!</i>

80
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:03,243
<i>Boss, please don't kill me!</i>
<i>I have a family!</i>

81
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:06,246
<i>I won't kill you</i>
<i>if you give me what I want.</i>

82
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:09,457
<i>You just have to tell me</i>
<i>all of the illegal activities</i>

83
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,042
<i>that Gov. Emilia Ardiente's involved in.</i>

84
00:04:14,545 --> 00:04:17,298
<i>Damn it! Tie him up! He's not talking.</i>

85
00:04:18,174 --> 00:04:20,843
[grunting]

86
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:26,683
[suspenseful music playing]

87
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:32,146
<i>He's not leaving this house</i>
<i>no matter what.</i>

88
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:35,316
<i>You will give him the clothes</i>
<i>he'll wear every day.</i>

89
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:38,111
<i>And don't forget to put this on him.</i>

90
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:41,572
<i>Put it somewhere where he won't notice.</i>

91
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:44,158
<i>-Copy?</i>
<i>-Yes, boss.</i>

92
00:04:51,165 --> 00:04:52,292
Hands behind your head.

93
00:04:55,336 --> 00:04:58,840
We're in the same profession.
Don't do anything stupid now.

94
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:00,341
Now hands behind your head!

95
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:04,679
Turn around.

96
00:05:09,642 --> 00:05:12,186
Just so you know, Tonio,
you're not getting away from me.

97
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:16,649
You will testify against Emilia Ardiente.

98
00:05:17,775 --> 00:05:18,985
Whether you like it or not.

99
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:26,534
[Carlotta] That Emilia is a parasite!

100
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:31,331
Nanny, don't worry.

101
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:36,669
Because the money I gave
will be the end of her.

102
00:05:37,962 --> 00:05:39,505
[phone rings]

103
00:05:43,009 --> 00:05:44,802
-<i>What do you want from me?</i>
-Shut up…

104
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:46,512
-What do you want from me?!
-<i>I said shut up!</i>

105
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,307
-Jepoy.
-Ivy.

106
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,435
I'll get him to talk. I promise.

107
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:55,938
[dramatic music playing]

108
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:10,536
I'm doing you a huge favor,
but you're just wasting it.

109
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,206
-You're not doing me any favors!
-Shut up!

110
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:19,796
How long have you been working
for the Ardientes?

111
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,715
I quit a long time ago.

112
00:06:23,591 --> 00:06:25,384
I changed because of my children!

113
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:27,929
[grunts]

114
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:31,057
Don't drag your kids into this!

115
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:35,978
Now, tell me.
What did you do to Camia Cruz?

116
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:41,484
Is Emilia's hit man going to confess now?

117
00:06:43,444 --> 00:06:44,487
I promise, Nanny.

118
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:47,156
I'll make sure Emilia goes to prison.

119
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:50,034
Just be strong, Ivy.

120
00:06:51,869 --> 00:06:53,955
I'll leave you to rest, all right?

121
00:06:57,625 --> 00:06:59,085
That's it!

122
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:02,130
If you don't talk now,

123
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:03,589
I'm going to bring your kids here

124
00:07:03,673 --> 00:07:06,509
and I'll send you all
to the Pearly Gates together!

125
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:07,510
Well?!

126
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:12,140
Well?!

127
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:15,017
I'll tell you everything.

128
00:07:17,311 --> 00:07:19,188
I started working as Emilia's hitman…

129
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:21,190
when she was still mayor.

130
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:24,986
I have a list of the people
she ordered me to kill.

131
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:34,829
[suspenseful music swells]

132
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:43,254
[instrumental theme music playing]

133
00:07:49,218 --> 00:07:51,179
[Lily] <i>They are the owners of that land.</i>

134
00:07:51,637 --> 00:07:54,140
<i>I just gave them back what's truly theirs.</i>

135
00:07:54,599 --> 00:07:55,766
<i>Ivy, thank you.</i>

136
00:07:57,101 --> 00:07:58,311
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

137
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:05,651
<i>It hurts, Diego, but I have</i>
<i>to stay away from you.</i>

138
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:10,323
<i>Especially now that my plans</i>
<i>are slowly unfolding.</i>

139
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:28,966
[instrumental theme music playing]

140
00:08:38,976 --> 00:08:43,064
[tense music playing]

141
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:57,912
Raul, where are you?

142
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:00,414
Are you here yet?

143
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:03,000
[Raul] <i>I don't think</i>
<i>I can make it there, Auntie.</i>

144
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:08,256
<i>Something came up.</i>
<i>Just keep an eye on her.</i>

145
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:12,093
<i>And don't let anyone in.</i>

146
00:09:12,176 --> 00:09:14,679
Wait, why? What happened?

147
00:09:15,846 --> 00:09:18,891
[tense music swelling]

148
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:27,900
[phone vibrating]

149
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:30,945
[soft, tense music playing]

150
00:09:37,451 --> 00:09:39,495
<i>I started working as Emilia's hit man</i>

151
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:42,248
<i>when… when she was still mayor.</i>

152
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:46,502
<i>I have a list of the people</i>
<i>she ordered me to kill.</i>

153
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:48,504
[Jepoy] <i>Are you the one</i>
<i>who killed Camia Cruz?</i>

154
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:52,925
<i>Answer me!</i>

155
00:09:54,051 --> 00:09:55,511
<i>Yes, I killed her!</i>

156
00:09:56,971 --> 00:10:02,602
<i>The governor ordered me</i>
<i>to rape and kill Camia Cruz!</i>

157
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:05,980
[tense music playing]

158
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:09,859
[phone rings]

159
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:11,944
-Ivy?
-<i>Jepoy.</i>

160
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:15,656
-Jepoy, I'm heading there.
-No, don't. We can't risk it.

161
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:18,951
<i>Listen to me, just this once.</i>

162
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:21,829
<i>Let me handle this.</i>

163
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:33,966
[dramatic music playing]

164
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:43,017
Hi, Madam.

165
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:46,646
I've deposited Miss Aguas' check
to your account.

166
00:10:46,729 --> 00:10:49,899
Good. What about the other check
I asked you to prepare?

167
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,108
Here it is.

168
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:57,907
[gushing] Brilliant, Lara!

169
00:10:58,199 --> 00:11:00,326
Okay, you may go now. Leave that here.

170
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:12,546
Hi, Arnaldo. Good morning.

171
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:15,174
What do you want for breakfast?
I'll have them cook it.

172
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:18,219
How about coffee? Did you sleep well?

173
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:19,678
I'm fine, Mom.

174
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,058
What's this for?

175
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:28,145
Oh, that's the check I'm going
to donate to the party.

176
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:32,108
150,000,000 pesos?

177
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:34,318
Where did you get that much money?

178
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:37,446
I sold the farmers' land to Ivy.

179
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:46,664
Coffee?

180
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:55,005
[Emilia] Ladies and gentlemen, senators…

181
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:59,009
thank you so much
for accepting my invitation.

182
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,512
I'm sure that you've heard or read

183
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:03,639
of the press releases I've issued.

184
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:04,974
[Pablo] Good job, Emilia.

185
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:08,644
I'm sure your approval rating
will skyrocket.

186
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:09,687
[giggles shyly]

187
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:13,649
Well, how about my rating in the party?

188
00:12:14,316 --> 00:12:15,818
[laughter]

189
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:18,946
Well, with that, I'd like to give you

190
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:21,365
my generous donation to the party.

191
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:22,450
Lara!

192
00:12:25,661 --> 00:12:26,871
[exhales in annoyance]

193
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,914
For the party.

194
00:12:29,248 --> 00:12:33,794
[applause]

195
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,629
-Congratulations, Emilia.
-Thank you, Senator.

196
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:38,215
Or shall I say, future Senator Ardiente?

197
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,885
Oh, thank you so much. [giggles]

198
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:49,351
-Congratulations.
-Thank you, Senator.

199
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:57,902
[Emilia] Thank you.

200
00:12:58,652 --> 00:13:01,280
[dramatic music playing]

201
00:13:03,365 --> 00:13:05,784
[tense music playing]

202
00:13:06,827 --> 00:13:09,121
-Bye-bye.
-Thank you, sir. Thank you.

203
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:10,956
Mom, I'll just take Natalie
and the senator home.

204
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,125
-All right. Bye, Natalie.
-We'll go ahead.

205
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:14,210
Thank you for coming.

206
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:22,718
-Emilia, I have to go now.
-Bye, Ivy? Oh, wait.

207
00:13:23,552 --> 00:13:25,888
Thank you so much for your help.

208
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,682
My senatorial dreams
are slowly coming true.

209
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:32,102
After that, it's the presidency.
How exciting, right?

210
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:35,940
[exhales] Emilia, don't get too excited.

211
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:38,359
Don't be so sure of yourself.

212
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,362
You haven't won yet.

213
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:47,243
And the party hasn't released an
official list of candidates yet.

214
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:51,080
There's still so much that can happen.

215
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:54,041
[tense music playing

216
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:56,794
I have to go.

217
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:09,473
Jepoy.

218
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,643
Have you taken care of everything?

219
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:15,145
Here's the video of Tonio's admission

220
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:18,440
to all of Emilia's crimes.

221
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:32,204
<i>Say goodbye to your dreams, Emilia.</i>

222
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:41,839
[Claire] For the success
of Senator Emilia.

223
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:43,924
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

224
00:14:46,927 --> 00:14:49,555
Hey, Raul, I don't wanna see you
with that long face tomorrow.

225
00:14:51,181 --> 00:14:54,268
That's right, Raul. You should
at least be happy for Emilia.

226
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:57,479
Well, of course.
I'm happy for Emilia. Very.

227
00:14:57,897 --> 00:14:58,898
Actually…

228
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:05,362
I've been waiting to give this.
Here's my gift for you.

229
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:09,700
Your favorite beauty products.
All for you.

230
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,328
Are you mocking me?

231
00:15:12,411 --> 00:15:15,873
[scoffs] No. I mean, think about this.

232
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:19,043
You're in politics, right?

233
00:15:19,126 --> 00:15:23,672
And all politicians age faster.
It's inevitable.

234
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:26,091
You're going to have a lot of
wrinkles. That's just how it is.

235
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:28,594
And I don't want that to happen to you.

236
00:15:28,844 --> 00:15:33,474
I mean, your constituents
call you Mommy Emilia right now,

237
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:36,435
but sooner or later,
they'll call you Grandma Emilia.

238
00:15:36,518 --> 00:15:37,937
[Raul] That doesn't sound good, right?

239
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,980
-Take your gift!
-Hold it!

240
00:15:40,689 --> 00:15:41,941
Can't you take a joke?

241
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:44,443
These are expensive. Loosen up, Emilia.

242
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:48,697
Go ahead, Raul. Mock me. Make fun of me.

243
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:50,074
Treat me like trash.

244
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:54,703
But if I win the senate race,
you'll regret all of this.

245
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:03,337
You should be more careful, my love.

246
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:07,967
Brace yourself for the worst,

247
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:12,388
because the higher your dreams are…

248
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,557
the harder you'll fall.

249
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:21,689
[tense music playing]

250
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:31,949
[Pablo] I know the party seems convinced

251
00:16:32,032 --> 00:16:34,159
that Emilia is going to replace
your grandfather.

252
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:38,122
But I assure you, Arnaldo,
you are going to get that spot.

253
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:41,166
Tomorrow's the announcement, Senator.

254
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,627
-What are you going to do?
-[scoffs]

255
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,255
Just trust me.

256
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:49,049
The question is…

257
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,887
Are you ready to go against
your own mother?

258
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:56,932
Because I'm telling you, Arnaldo…

259
00:16:57,516 --> 00:17:01,353
she's not going down without a fight.

260
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:16,660
As a child, this has always been my dream.

261
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:21,457
And I worked hard, worked as
hard as I can for this.

262
00:17:24,001 --> 00:17:26,545
It's difficult to be a woman in politics.

263
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:31,091
To be a wife, a mother.

264
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:35,471
But here I am. I made it.

265
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:39,600
I am Emilia Ardiente.

266
00:17:41,727 --> 00:17:46,523
I'm destined to be a queen,
and my reign starts today.

267
00:17:50,694 --> 00:17:54,323
[clapping continues]

268
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:03,749
[laughs lightly]

269
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:19,807
Thank you for this, Jepoy.

270
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:21,683
Thank you for everything you've done.

271
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:24,019
Don't mention it.

272
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,439
So, how are you doing?

273
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:31,276
I'm fine.

274
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:34,822
Did anyone bother you while I was away?

275
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:37,074
Did Diego try to make a move on you again?

276
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:44,123
I told you, Jepoy.
Diego apologized to me already.

277
00:18:45,999 --> 00:18:47,334
[ice clinking]

278
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,920
He even toured me around town.

279
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:54,007
The other day…

280
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:59,930
we went to the places
where we used to play.

281
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:04,977
Thirteen years.

282
00:19:06,603 --> 00:19:07,855
Jepoy, it's been 13 years.

283
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:12,401
But he still tells everyone
that I'm his best friend.

284
00:19:20,701 --> 00:19:22,578
I want all this to end.

285
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:26,456
So I can go back to living a normal life…

286
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:30,961
and be friends with Diego again.

287
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:37,551
Friends? Or lovers?

288
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:43,724
What kind of question is that?

289
00:19:46,226 --> 00:19:50,355
You better report back to Arnaldo.

290
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:52,107
I'm sure he's looking for you.

291
00:19:52,816 --> 00:19:54,318
Let's talk again tomorrow.

292
00:19:56,445 --> 00:19:57,654
Again, thanks for this.

293
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:05,954
Hey. Are you ready for tomorrow?

294
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:10,375
[tense music playing]

295
00:20:37,653 --> 00:20:38,654
Madrigal.

296
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:40,614
-Reporting for duty, Mayor.
-Good.

297
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:44,451
Where are we going today?

298
00:20:45,953 --> 00:20:47,162
To Senator Pablo's.

299
00:20:53,543 --> 00:20:54,503
-[door opens]

300
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:57,130
-Daddy.
-Hi, Natalie.

301
00:20:57,547 --> 00:21:00,217
-[singsong voice] Good morning.
-Good morning, darling.

302
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:02,970
I dropped by to give you this.

303
00:21:03,512 --> 00:21:05,514
It came in the mail earlier for you.

304
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:09,518
-Who's it from?
-I don't know. It doesn't say.

305
00:21:10,185 --> 00:21:14,982
Oh, Daddy, I have to go because
I have to check the event venue

306
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,817
for Auntie Emilia's things.

307
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:18,402
-All right, darling.
-I'll see you.

308
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:19,528
-Bye.
-[smooches]

309
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:21,071
Bye, Daddy.

310
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:37,879
[ominous music playing]

311
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:52,185
[ominous music swells]

312
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:57,691
[Emilia humming]

313
00:21:58,942 --> 00:22:02,195
[humming]

314
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:07,576
Raul, look! It suits me, right?
It sounds really nice.

315
00:22:07,784 --> 00:22:09,995
"Emilia is my senator!"

316
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:15,208
Come on, Raul.

317
00:22:15,292 --> 00:22:18,170
Can you at least pretend to be
happy when you're with me?

318
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:23,467
Look at me. I'm happy when I'm with you.

319
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:31,058
See that?

320
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:34,311
With you, it feels like I'm spending time…

321
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:36,813
with my pet dog.

322
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:39,107
-Hey!
-What did you say?!

323
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:40,942
[screams] Stop it! Hey!

324
00:22:41,193 --> 00:22:43,612
-[screams]
-Well?

325
00:22:43,695 --> 00:22:46,073
I've just about had it with you, Emilia.

326
00:22:46,323 --> 00:22:49,951
[grunts] Go ahead! Do it!

327
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:52,579
I dare you!

328
00:22:54,122 --> 00:22:58,043
I know you want me to fail,
but that won't happen.

329
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:02,339
For as long as I'm in power,
you will stay by my side.

330
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:04,091
What?!

331
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:21,942
[exhales]

332
00:23:24,319 --> 00:23:25,946
[cap clattering]

333
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:33,829
Senator, is everything okay?

334
00:23:34,121 --> 00:23:37,082
Ah, yes. Yes, of course.

335
00:23:40,585 --> 00:23:41,962
Good thing you're here.

336
00:23:44,339 --> 00:23:48,343
I'm very excited to tell you
that you got the vote.

337
00:23:49,636 --> 00:23:52,722
You will be running as senator.

338
00:23:54,474 --> 00:23:57,018
Uh… speaking of that.

339
00:23:57,602 --> 00:23:58,562
Uh…

340
00:23:58,895 --> 00:24:00,522
I'm backing out, Senator.

341
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:02,440
What?

342
00:24:03,733 --> 00:24:05,235
You cannot do that.

343
00:24:06,236 --> 00:24:08,321
You will run for senator.

344
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:10,574
That's the deal.

345
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:14,911
I pulled a lot of strings
for that endorsement.

346
00:24:15,370 --> 00:24:17,455
And now you're going
to chicken out like this?

347
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:18,999
-I understand.
-No!

348
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:21,459
No.

349
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:24,921
Now listen to me, Arnaldo.

350
00:24:25,922 --> 00:24:27,382
You can't back out.

351
00:24:28,341 --> 00:24:32,512
Because if you do that,
I will personally make sure…

352
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:38,226
that this is going to be the end
of your political career.

353
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:41,688
Is that clear?

354
00:24:46,401 --> 00:24:47,402
Go.

355
00:24:48,361 --> 00:24:49,821
Get ready for the party.

356
00:24:51,823 --> 00:24:53,200
Do this for Natalie.

357
00:24:53,992 --> 00:24:55,160
For your future.

358
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:08,006
[tense music swells]

359
00:25:09,466 --> 00:25:13,303
<i>Emilia's greed brought Julio down.</i>

360
00:25:16,806 --> 00:25:22,395
<i>Now, Arnaldo's greed</i>
<i>will do the same to Emilia.</i>

361
00:25:23,396 --> 00:25:24,940
<i>They're like dominoes.</i>

362
00:25:25,857 --> 00:25:29,694
<i>Push one down, you push them all down.</i>

363
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:34,532
I hope you're enjoying the party.

364
00:25:34,616 --> 00:25:36,451
-Senator.
-Oh. Excuse me.

365
00:25:36,993 --> 00:25:38,828
-Governor Emilia.
-Hi.

366
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:40,747
-How are you?
-Good, good.

367
00:25:40,830 --> 00:25:42,082
-Raul.
-Senator. Yeah.

368
00:25:42,165 --> 00:25:44,542
Oh, the senators would like
to have a word with you.

369
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:46,878
-All right. Hello, senators.
-Emilia.

370
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:49,631
-Senator Magno and Senator Jose.
-Of course, of course.

371
00:25:50,173 --> 00:25:52,425
Oh, Arnaldo. Excuse me.

372
00:25:52,968 --> 00:25:57,097
Arnaldo, where have you been all day?

373
00:25:57,180 --> 00:25:58,556
I've been looking for you at home.

374
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:01,643
We were already wondering
if you were going to show up.

375
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:03,061
I know. I'm-- I'm sorry.

376
00:26:03,144 --> 00:26:04,771
I just needed to take care of
something, Mom.

377
00:26:04,854 --> 00:26:06,231
[Natalie] He's so sweet, Auntie.

378
00:26:06,314 --> 00:26:09,442
He actually helped me organize
this whole event.

379
00:26:09,734 --> 00:26:11,778
Oh. Thank you, Natalie.

380
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:14,364
Oh, by the way. Where's Ivy?

381
00:26:19,411 --> 00:26:22,163
-There she is.
-[Ivy] Gov, I'm sorry I'm late.

382
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:25,917
Ivy, it's Senator, not Gov.

383
00:26:27,460 --> 00:26:28,753
Sorry, Senator.

384
00:26:29,129 --> 00:26:30,755
By the way, you look so great.

385
00:26:31,464 --> 00:26:32,966
[giggles] Thank you.

386
00:26:33,591 --> 00:26:35,510
Shall we get this party started?

387
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:37,178
-Sure.
-Let's go.

388
00:26:37,846 --> 00:26:40,056
Okay, I'm sorry. I'll just get a drink.

389
00:26:43,643 --> 00:26:48,023
Sorry, I stepped on your long…

390
00:26:48,606 --> 00:26:52,277
tacky metallic gown.

391
00:26:53,236 --> 00:26:55,822
What? Are you gonna sweep the floor?

392
00:26:55,905 --> 00:26:57,782
You're so thoughtful.

393
00:27:02,746 --> 00:27:04,914
You're so pretty, Natalie.

394
00:27:05,165 --> 00:27:08,209
But you shouldn't have worn your curtains.

395
00:27:09,419 --> 00:27:11,880
That's your comeback? Is that it?

396
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:15,133
[Magno] I agree with Miss Aguas.

397
00:27:15,383 --> 00:27:18,470
There should be a minimum
educational requirement

398
00:27:18,553 --> 00:27:20,889
for those who wish
to hold government positions.

399
00:27:21,514 --> 00:27:23,475
-[Jose] I'm a lawyer.
-[Pablo] Me, too.

400
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:28,563
Um, Emilia, we're friends,
but I still don't know

401
00:27:28,646 --> 00:27:30,065
where you graduated from.

402
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:32,525
Care to tell us?

403
00:27:33,401 --> 00:27:35,487
Um… abroad.

404
00:27:35,779 --> 00:27:39,574
Really? Where? From what university?

405
00:27:40,367 --> 00:27:44,621
Um… Wharton Business School, MBA.

406
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:47,248
-[Ivy] Top university.
-Mm-hm.

407
00:27:47,332 --> 00:27:49,084
Only a few select people
get to enroll there.

408
00:27:49,918 --> 00:27:51,252
Emilia is so humble

409
00:27:51,336 --> 00:27:54,547
to not list that
in her list of qualifications.

410
00:27:55,256 --> 00:27:57,842
[Pablo] What year did you
graduate there, Emilia?

411
00:27:58,218 --> 00:28:01,471
I know a professor there.
You might know him, too.

412
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:06,059
Come on, Senator. If I tell you
which year I graduated,

413
00:28:06,142 --> 00:28:07,894
it's like I'm telling you my real age,

414
00:28:07,977 --> 00:28:09,979
and I don't want that. [giggles]

415
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:12,482
Anyways, could you please excuse me?

416
00:28:12,565 --> 00:28:14,567
I just need to get ready
for my announcement.

417
00:28:14,651 --> 00:28:15,485
Excuse me.

418
00:28:20,698 --> 00:28:25,036
Wharton Business School?
I highly doubt it.

419
00:28:25,286 --> 00:28:27,080
[Magno] So, the rumors are true, then.

420
00:28:27,163 --> 00:28:29,124
Emilia didn't actually
graduate from college?

421
00:28:29,207 --> 00:28:34,379
Obviously, yes. That's why
we made the right call.

422
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:41,886
[Ivy] Excuse me. Senator Pablo.
So, what's your decision?

423
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:46,599
You'll see, Miss Aguas.

424
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:50,061
[tense music playing]

425
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:55,734
[Emilia sobbing]

426
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:01,906
[sobbing]

427
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:11,332
<i>I'll prove to you, bastards,</i>
<i>that I'm better than all of you.</i>

428
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:22,552
Mr. Mayor? Thank you.

429
00:29:22,635 --> 00:29:24,971
When it comes to service,
you are truly the best.

430
00:29:26,973 --> 00:29:28,183
I need your advice.

431
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:31,936
Can you hold this, please?

432
00:29:33,897 --> 00:29:36,274
How can I help you?

433
00:29:37,984 --> 00:29:38,818
It's about Mom.

434
00:29:40,195 --> 00:29:42,322
The party won't be choosing her tonight.

435
00:29:42,989 --> 00:29:43,990
What?

436
00:29:45,825 --> 00:29:47,577
But isn't that what you wanted?

437
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:49,078
Grandpa wanted it for me.

438
00:29:49,746 --> 00:29:51,331
I want it too, but…

439
00:29:52,165 --> 00:29:53,583
You're concerned about your mom.

440
00:29:54,334 --> 00:29:56,294
Because you know she'll be devastated.

441
00:29:57,587 --> 00:30:00,173
Well, knowing Emilia.

442
00:30:00,590 --> 00:30:03,134
And I'm sure you know
your mom very well, Arnaldo.

443
00:30:03,968 --> 00:30:06,262
She'll despise you for this.

444
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:08,723
Is that what you want?

445
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:14,479
It seems tonight, I don't have a choice.

446
00:30:15,855 --> 00:30:19,818
If I decline their endorsement,
the party will persecute me.

447
00:30:21,945 --> 00:30:23,196
I understand.

448
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:28,451
But you know, Arnaldo, you can
always choose another party.

449
00:30:29,702 --> 00:30:31,079
But you can never choose…

450
00:30:33,706 --> 00:30:34,707
your family.

451
00:30:39,462 --> 00:30:43,508
[tense music mellows]

452
00:30:43,633 --> 00:30:45,969
Senator Pablo Alcantara.

453
00:30:57,605 --> 00:30:58,815
Good evening.

454
00:30:59,357 --> 00:31:04,529
Tonight, we'll mark
another milestone for our party.

455
00:31:05,238 --> 00:31:07,740
It's a shame Julio's not here
to witness this.

456
00:31:08,491 --> 00:31:11,661
But I'm sure he will really be proud…

457
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:17,625
to see an Ardiente
in our senatorial lineup.

458
00:31:19,586 --> 00:31:25,091
His heir, who will follow
in his footsteps.

459
00:31:32,307 --> 00:31:34,767
I'm proud to present to you

460
00:31:34,851 --> 00:31:37,937
the person who will complete
the senatorial lineup

461
00:31:38,021 --> 00:31:41,107
of the Lakas Mamamayan Party.

462
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:43,151
A prolific leader.

463
00:31:44,110 --> 00:31:45,945
A young leader whose heart
is for the people.

464
00:31:49,490 --> 00:31:50,658
None other than…

465
00:31:55,705 --> 00:31:58,750
Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.

466
00:31:58,833 --> 00:32:02,921
[applause]

467
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:11,429
[tense music playing]

468
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:21,814
[tense music swells]

469
00:32:21,898 --> 00:32:22,941
[Arnaldo sighs]

470
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:38,331
Emilia…

471
00:32:51,719 --> 00:32:52,971
Thank you very much.

472
00:33:00,937 --> 00:33:03,356
It's a great honor
to be given this responsibility.

473
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:06,901
Honestly, I'm very excited

474
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:09,487
for the opportunity that you gave me.

475
00:33:15,785 --> 00:33:17,078
But I can't accept this.

476
00:33:21,499 --> 00:33:24,711
Governor Emilia will be taking
my grandfather's place.

477
00:33:32,260 --> 00:33:36,389
I'm sorry, but that is
the final decision of the party!

478
00:33:37,306 --> 00:33:41,394
Take it or leave
the Lakas Mamamayan Party.

479
00:33:42,103 --> 00:33:44,480
Well, Senator, if that's the case,

480
00:33:44,564 --> 00:33:46,524
then we will leave the political party.

481
00:33:48,943 --> 00:33:52,238
[dramatic music playing]

482
00:33:52,321 --> 00:33:55,116
Thank you so much, Senator,
for the memories,

483
00:33:55,199 --> 00:33:56,701
but no hard feelings.

484
00:33:57,452 --> 00:33:58,578
Shall we go, Arnaldo?

485
00:34:06,836 --> 00:34:09,172
<i>Two birds, one stone.</i>

486
00:34:09,255 --> 00:34:13,509
<i>Who's the better hunter now, Mr. Mayor?</i>

487
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:19,140
[tense music swells]

488
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:32,904
Governor, what can you say about this?

489
00:34:32,987 --> 00:34:35,573
-Governor, what happened?
-No comment.

490
00:34:35,656 --> 00:34:37,450
Shouldn't they have chosen you, Governor?

491
00:34:37,533 --> 00:34:39,494
You've got your scoop already.

492
00:34:40,203 --> 00:34:43,456
Governor, please tell us
why that happened.

493
00:34:43,873 --> 00:34:45,666
Senator, what's your comment on this?

494
00:34:47,460 --> 00:34:48,544
-Come on. Here!
-Daddy?

495
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:50,171
-Come here, Natalie.
-Daddy.

496
00:34:51,506 --> 00:34:54,383
-Let's go home.
-No, Daddy. What's happening?

497
00:34:54,467 --> 00:34:58,221
What is happening is that
you will break up with Arnaldo!

498
00:34:58,596 --> 00:35:02,141
No! That's not gonna happen,
Daddy. Are you crazy?

499
00:35:02,225 --> 00:35:04,310
We have no use for that family anymore.

500
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:06,646
They are going down, Natalie.

501
00:35:06,729 --> 00:35:08,981
And I won't let them drag us under!

502
00:35:10,149 --> 00:35:13,861
-I love Arnaldo, Daddy.
-Wake up, Natalie!

503
00:35:14,278 --> 00:35:18,157
He's just using you.
He will never love you.

504
00:35:18,241 --> 00:35:21,119
-No.
-Because he wants someone else.

505
00:35:21,202 --> 00:35:24,413
No, Daddy! [sobbing]

506
00:35:27,542 --> 00:35:28,960
This is Ivy's fault.

507
00:35:29,293 --> 00:35:33,047
This is Ivy's fault, Daddy.
She ruined everything.

508
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:37,218
-[groans]
-Natalie!

509
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:40,096
[growls]

510
00:35:42,223 --> 00:35:45,643
You ruined everything!

511
00:35:48,020 --> 00:35:52,984
You seduced Arnaldo to ruin our family.

512
00:35:54,694 --> 00:35:56,612
You ruined everything!

513
00:35:57,738 --> 00:36:00,324
[cries hysterically]

514
00:36:02,410 --> 00:36:03,411
[glass shatters]

515
00:36:05,955 --> 00:36:08,374
I will kill you!

516
00:36:10,459 --> 00:36:13,421
[grunting]

517
00:36:14,672 --> 00:36:17,967
A woman like you can't hurt me.

518
00:36:18,467 --> 00:36:21,137
I warned you. Don't try me!

519
00:36:22,096 --> 00:36:23,097
Move aside.

520
00:36:24,974 --> 00:36:26,184
[Natalie sobbing]

521
00:36:29,145 --> 00:36:31,230
I'm sorry, everyone. I have to go.

522
00:36:32,607 --> 00:36:33,608
Excuse me.

523
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:36,944
[Ivy] Excuse me.

524
00:36:47,246 --> 00:36:50,124
Emilia, Raul's gone.

525
00:36:50,917 --> 00:36:51,792
He left.

526
00:36:52,501 --> 00:36:55,296
Auntie, as of now,
I couldn't care less about him.

527
00:36:59,467 --> 00:37:02,511
[tense music plays]

528
00:37:02,595 --> 00:37:04,847
My only concern now is that traitor Pablo.

529
00:37:10,186 --> 00:37:11,437
What's your plan?

530
00:37:20,321 --> 00:37:21,656
[line ringing]

531
00:37:23,407 --> 00:37:24,742
[line ringing]

532
00:37:27,370 --> 00:37:28,579
-Raul.
-Auntie, how's everything?

533
00:37:28,663 --> 00:37:30,623
-Good thing you're here.
-Yes.

534
00:37:31,249 --> 00:37:32,583
She's in the room.

535
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:36,671
Thanks.

536
00:38:00,486 --> 00:38:02,321
IVY AGUAS FARMER'S HERO

537
00:38:14,917 --> 00:38:17,628
[Tonio] <i>I started working</i>
<i>as Emilia's hit man</i>

538
00:38:17,712 --> 00:38:20,047
<i>when… when she was still mayor.</i>

539
00:38:37,648 --> 00:38:40,609
<i>Your end is almost at hand, Emilia.</i>

540
00:38:40,985 --> 00:38:44,864
<i>I'll make sure you pay for your crimes.</i>

541
00:38:45,656 --> 00:38:48,034
<i>I swear it, Emilia.</i>

542
00:38:53,914 --> 00:38:57,043
We'll be leaving for Manila
first thing tomorrow, Natalie.

543
00:38:57,626 --> 00:38:59,211
Say your goodbyes to Arnaldo.

544
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:02,298
We're never returning here again.

545
00:39:08,554 --> 00:39:11,849
-What's going on?
-[car tires screeching]

546
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:13,642
[gunshots]

547
00:39:16,729 --> 00:39:18,814
-[gunshot]
-[groans]

548
00:39:33,704 --> 00:39:34,705
Good job.

549
00:39:38,292 --> 00:39:40,628
I assume you heard about what
happened to Senator Alcantara,

550
00:39:40,711 --> 00:39:42,296
and I can see you're already celebrating.

551
00:39:43,130 --> 00:39:46,425
Don't you like that? That's one
less problem to deal with.

552
00:39:49,637 --> 00:39:51,138
[phone ringing]

553
00:39:52,264 --> 00:39:53,682
[phone ringing]

554
00:39:55,267 --> 00:39:56,227
Jepoy?

555
00:39:56,644 --> 00:39:59,021
Hello, Ivy. It's about Senator Alcantara.

556
00:39:59,438 --> 00:40:00,648
Why? What happened?

557
00:40:01,148 --> 00:40:02,191
He was ambushed, Ivy.

558
00:40:03,776 --> 00:40:04,902
He's dead.

559
00:40:08,948 --> 00:40:11,534
Jepoy, we need to move faster.

560
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:13,661
<i>I won't let Emilia order her men to kill…</i>

561
00:40:13,744 --> 00:40:15,246
any more people than she already has.

562
00:40:15,496 --> 00:40:16,705
Tonio is our key.

563
00:40:17,039 --> 00:40:21,752
He will expose Emilia
for everything she's done.

564
00:40:22,128 --> 00:40:23,921
<i>And he will do that in court.</i>

565
00:40:24,296 --> 00:40:26,132
Make sure you do everything
I asked you to.

566
00:40:26,799 --> 00:40:28,050
Don't worry, Ivy.

567
00:40:28,717 --> 00:40:30,553
Just like what I promised Miss Prianka…

568
00:40:32,012 --> 00:40:33,764
I'll do everything to help you succeed.

569
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:35,808
Thank you.

570
00:40:49,947 --> 00:40:53,451
Wow, you seem to be in high spirits today.

571
00:40:53,742 --> 00:40:56,912
Have your prayers been answered, Emilia?

572
00:40:56,996 --> 00:40:57,913
[laughs]

573
00:40:58,038 --> 00:41:00,791
Well, Auntie Clarita, you can say that

574
00:41:00,875 --> 00:41:03,752
I'm slowly getting closer to what I want.

575
00:41:04,420 --> 00:41:08,966
It's Claire. I want you
to call me Claire, Emilia.

576
00:41:09,133 --> 00:41:12,595
Auntie Clarita, Claire.
It's just the same, Auntie.

577
00:41:12,970 --> 00:41:17,600
Your niece is still going to be
a senator very soon.

578
00:41:17,725 --> 00:41:21,312
And I won't get that
by just praying, Auntie.

579
00:41:23,189 --> 00:41:26,275
So, what are you up to, my dear niece?

580
00:41:27,443 --> 00:41:32,281
Well, Auntie, no one can stop me
from running for Senate.

581
00:41:32,615 --> 00:41:35,201
Not even that stupid political party.

582
00:41:35,576 --> 00:41:37,995
I know all my strengths and weaknesses.

583
00:41:38,913 --> 00:41:41,332
That's why I need Ivy Aguas.

584
00:41:42,458 --> 00:41:47,671
I need her influence, her power,
and most importantly, her money.

585
00:41:48,923 --> 00:41:51,008
And thanks to Arnaldo,

586
00:41:51,091 --> 00:41:53,928
I can play that woman like a puppet.

587
00:42:06,899 --> 00:42:10,486
[tense music playing]

588
00:42:19,954 --> 00:42:24,500
<i>I will never lose you again,</i>
<i>no matter what.</i>

589
00:42:25,459 --> 00:42:26,460
<i>Because you're mine.</i>

590
00:42:33,842 --> 00:42:36,637
-[panting]
-<i>Mom? What happened to you?</i>

591
00:42:36,720 --> 00:42:38,514
-[shushes]
-[Tonio] <i>Hey!</i>

592
00:42:38,806 --> 00:42:42,184
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

593
00:42:42,268 --> 00:42:45,896
<i>Where's my mom?</i>
<i>You said you'd take me to her.</i>

594
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:51,860
<i>Mom, what did they do to you?</i>

595
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:55,573
<i>Mom!</i>

596
00:42:56,156 --> 00:42:57,324
<i>Lily?</i>

597
00:42:58,450 --> 00:43:01,453
<i>Lily, my dear? Please, help me.</i>

598
00:43:03,122 --> 00:43:06,542
<i>-Mom, where are you? Mom?</i>
<i>-Lily, help me!</i>

599
00:43:06,625 --> 00:43:09,461
<i>-Mom?</i>
<i>-Lily. Lily!</i>

600
00:43:13,048 --> 00:43:14,049
<i>Mom?</i>

601
00:43:15,342 --> 00:43:16,343
<i>Lily.</i>

602
00:43:16,969 --> 00:43:18,470
<i>-Mom.</i>
<i>-Lily.</i>

603
00:43:18,721 --> 00:43:21,223
<i>-Mom.</i>
<i>-Lily, help me.</i>

604
00:43:23,642 --> 00:43:24,643
<i>Lily.</i>

605
00:43:28,147 --> 00:43:29,189
<i>Mom.</i>

606
00:43:31,066 --> 00:43:32,067
<i>Mom?</i>

607
00:43:33,152 --> 00:43:34,528
<i>-Mom!</i>
<i>-Lily.</i>

608
00:43:36,905 --> 00:43:37,781
<i>Mom.</i>

609
00:43:38,949 --> 00:43:39,950
<i>Mom?</i>

610
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:42,578
<i>-Mom!</i>
<i>-Lily.</i>

611
00:43:43,537 --> 00:43:45,039
<i>Lily, help me.</i>

612
00:43:45,998 --> 00:43:47,541
<i>I will, Mom. Mom.</i>

613
00:43:51,462 --> 00:43:52,963
<i>Mom!</i>

614
00:43:53,714 --> 00:43:56,884
[tense music playing]

615
00:43:57,259 --> 00:43:58,260
[quietly] Mom.

616
00:44:11,899 --> 00:44:15,903
[tense music swells]

617
00:44:30,626 --> 00:44:33,754
Ivy, does Nanny Carlotta know about this?

618
00:44:33,921 --> 00:44:35,923
She left early for the market today.

619
00:44:36,215 --> 00:44:38,759
-Come on, Ivy.
-Jepoy, this feels different.

620
00:44:39,176 --> 00:44:41,095
-Is it because of your dream?
-Yes.

621
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:43,180
I don't know.

622
00:44:43,639 --> 00:44:47,142
All I know is I want to see Tonio myself.

623
00:44:47,768 --> 00:44:50,354
Because I'm not
just searching for justice,

624
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:53,899
but for the truth as well.
That's why I need to see Tonio.

625
00:44:58,654 --> 00:44:59,488
Are you ready?

626
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:02,116
I just want to make sure, Ivy.

627
00:45:02,991 --> 00:45:05,327
Are you ready to face the person
who killed your mother?

628
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:07,704
That's what I want to know, Jepoy.

629
00:45:08,163 --> 00:45:11,333
I want to make sure
if my mom really is dead.

630
00:45:13,001 --> 00:45:14,420
And if she is dead,

631
00:45:14,628 --> 00:45:16,130
I want to know how he killed her.

632
00:45:16,463 --> 00:45:18,298
I want answers to everything.

633
00:45:18,382 --> 00:45:21,969
Because I want the Ardientes
to pay exactly what they owe me.

634
00:45:24,054 --> 00:45:25,139
Including Diego?

635
00:45:28,892 --> 00:45:29,935
I'm coming with you.

636
00:45:40,237 --> 00:45:42,406
[car engine revs]

637
00:45:42,489 --> 00:45:45,868
[suspenseful music playing]

638
00:45:49,538 --> 00:45:51,832
[music fades]

639
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:03,177
Jepoy, thank you.

640
00:46:08,557 --> 00:46:09,933
I know I make…

641
00:46:11,727 --> 00:46:13,353
a lot of risky decisions.

642
00:46:15,355 --> 00:46:16,899
Decisions that…

643
00:46:19,443 --> 00:46:20,652
make you worry.

644
00:46:22,571 --> 00:46:23,947
But you're still here.

645
00:46:26,033 --> 00:46:30,120
Ever since you rescued me
from that perverted driver…

646
00:46:31,205 --> 00:46:34,082
you've always been there for me.

647
00:46:34,291 --> 00:46:37,085
You never left me. Thank you so much.

648
00:46:40,422 --> 00:46:41,673
You saved me too, Ivy.

649
00:46:42,633 --> 00:46:44,510
From my life in the streets.

650
00:46:46,220 --> 00:46:49,014
Both you and Miss Prianka.
I owe you both my life.

651
00:46:50,015 --> 00:46:53,268
That makes us even then.

652
00:46:55,229 --> 00:46:59,816
I helped you because
you're a good friend, Jepoy.

653
00:47:00,150 --> 00:47:04,488
To be honest, you do so much for me.

654
00:47:04,863 --> 00:47:11,078
Sometimes, you risk your life
posing as one of Arnaldo's men.

655
00:47:12,371 --> 00:47:14,164
But you're always there when I need you.

656
00:47:15,791 --> 00:47:17,501
You do all those things for me…

657
00:47:18,210 --> 00:47:21,338
to help me seek justice for my parents.

658
00:47:22,881 --> 00:47:23,966
So, Jepoy…

659
00:47:26,260 --> 00:47:27,261
thank you.

660
00:47:30,305 --> 00:47:33,392
[soft music playing]

661
00:47:36,812 --> 00:47:40,566
[suspenseful music swells]

662
00:47:46,071 --> 00:47:47,281
Tonio's inside.

663
00:47:58,125 --> 00:48:02,004
[action music playing]

664
00:48:20,230 --> 00:48:21,231
Open it.

665
00:48:30,407 --> 00:48:31,658
[doors squeak open]

666
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:35,954
[action music continues playing]

667
00:48:40,959 --> 00:48:44,921
[action music swells]

668
00:48:45,255 --> 00:48:50,552
[dramatic music playing]

669
00:49:01,647 --> 00:49:03,815
<i>How did you kill Camia Cruz?!</i>

670
00:49:03,899 --> 00:49:05,859
<i>She was still alive</i>
<i>when I buried her in the forest.</i>

671
00:49:05,942 --> 00:49:06,777
<i>Please forgive me.</i>

672
00:49:06,860 --> 00:49:10,155
<i>That word means nothing to me now.</i>

673
00:49:10,238 --> 00:49:12,491
<i>Everything you've worked</i>
<i>so hard for is crumbling down.</i>

674
00:49:12,574 --> 00:49:14,242
<i>I don't know what to do. I need you.</i>

675
00:49:14,326 --> 00:49:15,869
[machine beeping]

676
00:49:15,952 --> 00:49:17,371
[Diego] <i>Why is she always with Mom?</i>

677
00:49:17,454 --> 00:49:18,789
<i>What does she need from my family?</i>

678
00:49:18,872 --> 00:49:19,998
<i>Why is she in Poblacion Ardiente?</i>

679
00:49:20,082 --> 00:49:22,292
[Loring] <i>Let's say that she is Lily.</i>

680
00:49:22,376 --> 00:49:24,044
<i>Then why does she need to pretend?</i>

681
00:49:24,127 --> 00:49:25,253
<i>That's what I have to find out.</i>

682
00:49:25,337 --> 00:49:27,714
[man] <i>Let's just wait for the</i>
<i>results of the DNA test.</i>

683
00:49:27,798 --> 00:49:29,883
<i>I need the results in 24 hours.</i>

684
00:49:31,093 --> 00:49:33,845
<i>I'm going to find you, Mom…</i>

685
00:49:34,179 --> 00:49:37,224
[theme music playing]
